<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pomeranians (Slavic tribe)</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Slavic Pomeranians</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pomeranians were a West Slavic people who lived along the Baltic coast between the Oder and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vistula">Vistula</a> in the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>. Their tribes were united under local dukes such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wartislaw-i-duke-of-pomerania">Wartislaw I</a> and converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-of-bamberg">Otto of Bamberg</a> in the 1120s. Over the following centuries most were assimilated by German settlers, though the Kashubians descend from them.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pomeranians-slavic-tribe.jpg" alt="Pomeranians (Slavic tribe)" width="320" height="264" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Piotrus · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:West_slavs_9th-10th_c..png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
